# Codex config

## Canonical layout

- Source: `~/src/boilerplate/home/`
- Live files: `{{ .decentangl.defaults.codex_home }}/`

## Current target

{{ template "codex/current-target.md.tmpl" . }}

## Invariants

- Edit source in a worktree of the canonical checkout (`decent-angl-config`),
  never `{{ .decentangl.defaults.codex_home }}/`.
- Keep auth, history, caches, sqlite files, logs, and project trust local.
- T3 Code extra accounts use an empty shadow home under `~/.codex-t3/`.
  Never copy `~/.codex` into it. Login with `codex-t3-second login`.
- Shared Astra policy: `home/.chezmoitemplates/codex/model-policy.toml.tmpl`.
  It manages the default model, parent reasoning effort, service tier, subagent
  defaults, context overrides, and experimental context flag across independent
  runtime configs. Preserve other local settings.
- CLI pin: `home/dot_config/mise/config.toml`. T3 uses `codex-baseline` for
  every account. Desktop runtime versions are separate from the CLI pin.
- Keep global `AGENTS.md` out of default context. Durable workflow lives in skills.
- Render platform or host differences with templates. Move repeated mechanics
  into manifest-driven scripts.

## Workflow

1. Run `decent-angl-sync status`, then edit `home/...` in a worktree
   (`git -C ~/src/boilerplate worktree add ~/src/boilerplate-wt/<task>`).
2. Preview with `chezmoi -S ~/src/boilerplate-wt/<task> diff`.
3. Commit, land with `git merge --ff-only` in `~/src/boilerplate`, then run
   `decent-angl-sync reconcile`: it validates the committed snapshot's OMP
   agent policy, publishes, and applies. Verify rendered files and
   `codex --version`.
